},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡{90}^{∘}=0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡{0}^{∘}=1.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{90}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{0}^{∘} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+0+1 & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}+2}{2}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527930 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527930 #edb/ref 1069 "q-266630" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527930 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527930 #edb/ref 1071 "$6\\operatorname{sec}⁡{60}^{∘}+3\\operatorname{csc}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cot}⁡{30}^{∘}=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527930 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3ac560de-8de4-5482-a34a-4c1b0b94d0a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527930 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that $sec$  is the reciprocal of $cos,$  $csc$ is the reciprocal of $sin$  and $cot$  is the reciprocal of $tan.$\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}},\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}}.\n$$\n\nThe angle ${60}^{∘}$ and ${30}^{∘}$ are special, and its trigonometric ratios have the values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{sec}⁡{60}^{∘}+3\\operatorname{csc}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cot}⁡{30}^{∘} & = \\\\ 6(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}})+3(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}})+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}}+\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡{30}^{∘}} & = \\\\ \\frac{6}{(\\frac{1}{2})}+\\frac{3}{(\\frac{1}{2})}+\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})} & = \\\\ 12+6+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ 18+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ 18+\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} & = \\\\ 18+\\sqrt{3}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527931 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527931 #edb/ref 1069 "q-5987" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527931 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527931 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527931 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3e80bab2-07dc-55db-9807-7a129c6e1f5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527931 #edb/ref 1074 "The angles ${30}^{∘}$ and ${60}^{∘}$ are special, and their trigonometric ratios have the  values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & = \\\\ 0 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527940 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527940 #edb/ref 1069 "q-244570" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527940 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527940 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡{0}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡{60}^{∘}=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527940 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5201241f-04a1-5e84-80f6-a8d23279f733" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527940 #edb/ref 1074 "The angles of ${0}^{∘},\\,{30}^{∘},$ and ${60}^{∘}$ are special, and their trigonometric ratios have the particular values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{0}^{∘}=0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{0}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡{60}^{∘} & = \\\\ 0+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\sqrt{3} & = \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527953 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527953 #edb/ref 1069 "q-4761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527953 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527953 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/44/4456324cb31f62f0d856bc71b0f0a1e8f68e2b0ae0a8e9148e4d4dde9c4aca7d.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡H=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527953 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6daa4c32-448d-5d51-8b4c-73d314338ef5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527953 #edb/ref 1074 "We have that $m∠H={45}^{∘},$ which is a special angle. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡H & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527959 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527959 #edb/ref 1069 "q-28653" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527959 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527959 #edb/ref 1071 "$5{cos}^{2}⁡{45}^{∘}+3{sin}^{2}⁡{45}^{∘}-7{tan}^{2}⁡{45}^{∘}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527959 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7bdb766f-cf3d-53c5-a841-7b6efda706a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527959 #edb/ref 1074 "The angle ${45}^{∘}$ is special, and its trigonometric ratios have the values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘}=1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nAlso, note that ${sin}^{2}⁡{45}^{∘}$ means $(\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘})^{2},$ ${cos}^{2}⁡{45}^{∘}$ means $(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘})^{2}$ and  ${tan}^{2}⁡{45}^{∘}$ means $(\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘})^{2}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{cos}^{2}⁡{45}^{∘}+3{sin}^{2}⁡{45}^{∘}-7{tan}^{2}⁡{45}^{∘} & = \\\\ 5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘})^{2}+3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘})^{2}-7(\\operatorname{tan}⁡{45}^{∘})^{2} & = \\\\ 5{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}+3{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}-7(1)^{2} & = \\\\ 8{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}-7 & = \\\\ 8(\\frac{2}{4})-7 & = \\\\ 4-7 & = \\\\ -3. & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527990 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527990 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76758" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527990 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527990 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡{0}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527990 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c582da59-32d5-5633-9b42-0c1f59213de1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527990 #edb/ref 1074 "The angles ${0}^{∘}$ and ${30}^{∘}$ are special angles, and their trigonometric ratios have the values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{0}^{∘}=0,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{0}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} & = \\\\ 0+\\frac{1}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
